# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This repo is a TEMPLATE. It tracks the memory system itself and nothing the
# memory system produces, so a clone starts empty and `git status` stays quiet
# while you actually use it.
#
# Tracked:   hooks/, mcp_server.py, settings.json, .mcp.json, CLAUDE.md, README
# Ignored:   everything below, all of it generated per install
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Generated memory data. Covers the episodic tiers (tier0, tier1, tier2, ...),
# the whole narrative track (draft, chapter, book, collection), the semantic
# files (preferences, antipatterns, skillTree, prefs, project) and every
# auto-generated skill under semantic/skills/. Also catches the .pending.md
# sidecars that compression parks while a summary is being validated.
.claude/memory/**/*.md

# Compression runtime state (not .md, so the rule above misses them)
.claude/memory/.compress.lock
.claude/memory/.compress_state.json

# Logs: hook debug capture (events.log), compression, semantic extraction
*.log

# Per-project docs - written per install, not shipped with the template
whitepaper.md
roadmap.md

# Local settings and backup/scratch files
.claude/settings.local.json
*.bak
*.bak.*

# Windows artifact from a stray `> nul` redirect
nul

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Salvaged reference material, kept locally and never shipped to a clone
.reference/

# Snapshots taken before normalizing memory layers by hand. Generated data
# like .claude/memory itself, and specific to one install's history.
.claude/memory_backups/

# This project's own working docs - a clone starts its own, it doesn't inherit these
PLAN_memory_improvements.md
requirements.txt
